   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the social services law, in relation to requiring the office\nof temporary and disability assistance to make publicly available on its\nwebsite information regarding waivers, rental supplement plans and shelter\nsupplement plans",
    "basePrintNo": "S9343",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S9343-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §152-e, Soc Serv L",
    "lawSection": "Social Services Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S9343\n\nSPONSOR: PERSAUD\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the social services law, in relation to requiring the\noffice of temporary and disability assistance to make publicly available\non its website information regarding waivers, rental supplement plans\nand shelter supplement plans\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo amend the insurance law, requiring the Department of Financial\nServices to publish a report on long-term care insurance rates.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Amends the insurance law by adding a new section 204 requir-\ning the department of financial services to publish a report on longterm\ncare insurance rates.\n\nSection 2: Sets the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill would require the Department of Financial Services to post\nlongterm care rate increases from the past 10 years on their website in\nan easily accessible manner. As the population ages and long-term care\ncosts continue to rise, consumers' access to reliable and affordable LTC\ninsurance is critically important.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nOn the ninetieth day after it shall become law.\n",
    "multiSponsors": {
